    "body": "<p><strong><a href=\"https://generativehistory.substack.com/p/gpt-62-astra-solves-a-historical\">GPT 6.2 Astra Solves a Historical Mystery</a></strong></p> Here's an interesting case-study in using GPT-6.2 Astra for historical research, from history professor Mark Humphries:</p> <blockquote> <p>With only minimal prompting, GPT-6.2 Astra was able to autonomously identify the creator of an anonymous 1808 sketchbook held at <a href=\"https://beinecke.library.yale.edu/\">Yale’s Beinecke Library</a>. It did so extremely quickly (in just 22 minutes), using publicly available primary and secondary sources. To do so, it discovered a little known source in a paper archive, predicted that it would prove its hypothesis if examined and, in the end, it did. Not only that, but this new source turns out to b",
